             :plan "For held task `seon.ref/define-a-pathless-reference-section-is-a-missing-file-error` the raw `seon.context/current-state` block is about 38 k characters (about 9.5 k tokens, inferred as characters/4): task 2300, chain 1134, proofs 2218, step 103, must-reads 31485, turns 88 (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/sci-reuse-across-tasks.md#4-seoncontextcurrent-state-regeneration`). Must-reads are 83% of it. The AI view's size after the must-reads' declared renders was not measured: measure it first and state it in tokens. What the work must be proportional to: what the agent needs to start (the task, its proofs and each reference's essence), with detail one requery away. The planned fix is TASK-CHAIN's doc views (`docs/seon/schedule/cards/TASK-CHAIN.md#3a-agent-verbs-and-what-references-show`): render a reference as the section it names, not the whole file. Done when the rendered block for that probe is under a stated token budget that is a config dial, with each cut naming its elision form. Proof: to write before assignment."}
